# Capability YAML under this directory is checked out with LF on every
# platform. Two starter files are embedded into the binary with include_str!
# (src/commands/mod.rs), so a Windows build from a CRLF checkout would ship
# them with CRLF bytes. The pin hash reads CRLF as LF either way
# (src/capability/hash.rs); this keeps the embedded bytes identical across
# release targets. It lives here, not at the root, because the root file
# allowlist (scripts/dev/check-public-repo-hygiene.sh) is closed.
*.yaml text eol=lf
